# PIRTM — Prime-Indexed Recursive Tensor Mathematics

**A verified contractive recurrence runtime with a compile-time MLIR dialect.**

Canonical PIRTM implementation authority: https://github.com/MultiplicityFoundation/PIRTM
This `Tooling/pirtm` tree is a live implementation surface and runtime host, but canonical semantic and implementation authority remains in the standalone PIRTM repository.

PIRTM is the L0 (core-foundations) layer of the Tooling workspace.  Every
session in the system must be *proven contractive* before it executes.
Contractivity is verified in two temporal phases:

- **Transpile-time** (`contractivity-check`) — per-module, checked when
  `.pirtm.bc` bytecode is produced.
- **Link-time** (`spectral-small-gain`) — network-wide, checked when
  modules are linked into a session graph.

PIRTM is developed with a math-first discipline.  The recurrence relation,
modulus constraints, operator norms, and spectral bounds are the primary
artifacts; implementations exist to realize those artifacts faithfully.
Tests are treated as executable certificates that each operation respects its
mathematical contract under valid inputs, invalid inputs, and composition.

**Current status**: Phase 4 (LLVM + Standalone Runtime), 6 of 7 compilation
gates passed (Day 90 performance benchmark in progress).  Gate K
(Multiplicity-LWE runtime hardening) is complete — K-01 through K-05 all
carry passing production-grade evidence suites (108 tests across Gate K
alone).

---

