## Tests

PIRTM tests are certification artifacts.  They are meant to witness that the
runtime, verifier, transpiler, and linker satisfy their mathematical contracts:
prime typing, squarefree composite handling, contractive recurrence behavior,
stable diagnostics, link-time spectral bounds, and bytecode inspection rules.

```
pirtm/tests/
├── fixtures/                       .pirtm.bc files + fixture generator
├── pirtm-types-basic.mlir           Day 0-3 MLIR diagnostic test
├── mlir_diagnostic_verifier.py      Python-based MLIR diagnostic simulator
│
│   — Core compilation gates —
├── test_dialect_types.py            Type-layer unit tests
├── test_day_3_7_coprime_merge.py    Coprime merge + grep gates
├── test_day_7_14_round_trip.py      Transpiler round-trip
├── test_day_14_contractivity.py     Bytecode + inspection
├── test_commitment_collision.py     Duplicate identity_commitment (Day 14-16)
├── test_spectral_gates.py           Network stability: r=0.7 / r=1.1
├── test_phase4_integration.py       End-to-end Phase 4
├── test_predictive_warnings.py      Margin prediction
├── test_module_reordering.py        Margin-driven reordering
│
│   — Gate K (Multiplicity-LWE runtime) —
├── test_multiplicity_lwe_params.py  K-01: parameter validation and prime checks
├── test_multiplicity_lwe_api.py     K-01: LWE API surface
├── test_k02_multiplicity_core.py    K-02: MultiplicityCoreEngine + contraction harness
├── test_k03_boundary_contract.py    K-03: ProtectedEngine boundary contract
├── test_k04_csl_gate.py             K-04: CSLGate 53-case failure-mode matrix
├── test_k05_rate_limiter.py         K-05: RateLimiter + adversarial convergence
├── test_gate_k_integration_smoke.py End-to-end Gate K controller smoke test
│
│   — Tooling —
├── test_render_gate_k_status.py     Status renderer derivation regression (28 tests)
├── test_standalone_packaging.py     Packaging boundary regression
└── ...                              (56 test files total)
```

Run the full PIRTM test suite:

```bash
pytest pirtm/tests/ -v
```

When adding a feature, the minimum certification set should cover:

- the governing equation or invariant,
- boundary and degenerate cases,
- rejection behavior with deterministic diagnostics,
- composition with neighboring stages in the pipeline,
- regression coverage for any bug or counterexample that motivated the change.

